",\n          \"text\": \"Photos and videos are almost always the biggest storage hog. Start there with a dedicated cleanup tool like TidyByte to remove duplicates, blurry shots, and old screenshots. Next, go to Settings > General > iPhone Storage to see a ranked list of apps by size and offload or delete the ones you rarely use. Finally, clear Safari cache, delete old message threads with large attachments, and empty your Recently Deleted album to reclaim the last few gigabytes.\"\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n  </script>\n",
